3.1 Amapiano, Bacardi & Cultural Dance Challenges
South African dance challenges travel rapidly from local townships to global timelines, giving players unmistakable physical routines to act out1. A premier card is the Bacardi Dance (widely called the "Tyla Dance" on TikTok after Tyla popularized it alongside her hit "Water", though Bona Magazine notes she stated in an interview that she prefers its original name, the Bacardi dance)9. Another staple is the "Kwenzekalani" Amapiano Dance Challenge (2024), which GQ South Africa reports gained massive traction when Cassper Nyovest and his wife Thobeka Majozi, alongside DJs Kabza De Small and DJ Maphorisa, showcased their moves on TikTok35. Players can also act out the "Tshwala Bam" Dance Challenge (by TitoM & Yuppe, a 2024 Song of the Year nominee), the "Mnike" (Tyler ICU) and "Dalie" (Kamo Mphela) challenges, or the Traditional Zulu Cultural Dance Challenge, which Bona Magazine highlights for spawning two contrasting TikTok versions: an energetic original with high leg-raises and a ultra-graceful version where dancers barely lift their legs off the floor9. For verbal-physical comedy, include the "Off Course" Challenge (2024), which South Africans localized with vernacular humor and everyday twists, even catching the attention of Will Smith35.
